{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470846-buffing-yourself-before-combat","id":1470846,"title":"Buffing yourself before combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-19T06:36:15-08:00","id":1470846,"title":"Buffing yourself before combat","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> Im looking for ideas for before-combat &quot;buffing&quot; spells/rotes for my NPCs. The ones mages can keep working on themselves for a whole fight. <br /> <br /> Besides<br /> Life 3 to improve your physical atributes,<br /> Correspondence 1 to decrease the difficulty of your moves by sensing the space, <br /> Prime 2 to reinforce your clothing<br /> Mind 1 to keep your mind protected<br /> <br /> I dont know what else. I appreciate your input and thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T08:36:53-08:00","id":1470857,"title":"","content":"What spheres are available?<br /> Anyway, you can add successes in damage with Forces as well as decrease them (shield).<br /> You can also increase the difficulty of enemies hitting you by several ways.<br /> Also, use Prime or Forces to make your damage aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T13:51:08-08:00","id":1470880,"title":"","content":"Any spheres available. Im looking for general ideas for NPCs, mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:41:25-08:00","id":1470887,"title":"","content":"Any spheres levels? Paradigms?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Regeneration - Life 2 (Increased regeneration or reduced recovery time)</li> <li>Aztec ritual - Life/Spirit/Prime 5 (Let the magician sacrifice someone and pull out the heart and give himself / a friend / item bonus 3 quintessences per success)</li> <li>Infernal blessing - Spirit 3, Life 2 (or 3-4?), Prime 1 (Make a sacrifice to a god and receive temporary blessing from your god. Maybe the god of war will give bonus 2 points in a skill or attribute, or the god of the sea / rain will give the ability to breathe underwater)</li> <li>Confirmation aura - Entropy 5 (Take your desired shape/costume/image/mask - with every attack enemies will be convinced that you are a great warrior)</li> <li>Warp-shape - Life 3, Prime 4 (Mutation that will add muscle mass, increase hormone levels and adrenaline levels. You need a strong will to resist the impulses of the berserker)</li> <li>Mirage - Force 2, Life 3, Prime 3 (Create a distortion of light around your body)</li> <li>Stone flesh - Matter 2, Life 4, Prime 3 (We bury ourselves in a forest / swamp / river - climb out with stones / roots in our body and get +1/2 armor or 1 stamina. But your pretty face is finished)</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-21-2021, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T05:31:06-08:00","id":1470928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470846-buffing-yourself-before-combat?p=1470880#post1470880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any spheres available. Im looking for general ideas for NPCs, mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically you can:<br /> <br /> - increase your attacker difficulty to hit you<br /> - decrease your dodge difficulty<br /> - increase your dmg successes<br /> - decrease your attacker dmg successes<br /> - buff your attributes<br /> - become invisible<br /> - decrease your soak difficulty<br /> -make you soak lethal/aggravated<br /> <br /> <br /> When in combat you can also:<br /> <br /> - nerf your attacker atributes<br /> - remove attacker senses (blindness, deafening)<br /> - increase attacker soak difficulty<br /> - paralyze attacker<br /> <br /> I believe you can also increase/decrease dices, but we don't have this in M20.<br /> <br /> About how to do them, there are infinite ways with probably every sphere. Some spheres, like Forces, can do all of them.<br /> <br /> That's all I can think right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T10:52:52-08:00","id":1471093,"title":"","content":"In Revised, Entropy 1 allows you to decrease the difficulty of damage rolls. I don't think the text allows for this in M20 however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T17:16:26-08:00","id":1471116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470846-buffing-yourself-before-combat?p=1471093#post1471093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Revised, Entropy 1 allows you to decrease the difficulty of damage rolls. I don't think the text allows for this in M20 however.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 doesn't mention this. But unless there is a new rule contradicting an old one, then the old one is still running. Sometimes you can even use old rules over new ones, especially if the new one suck (familiars...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T17:06:31-08:00","id":1471217,"title":"","content":"Matter 3 to bolster your regular clothing, granting it dots of Armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T07:48:29-08:00","id":1471532,"title":"","content":"My Wu Lung Character Hu had a bunch of combat buffs. Here are three of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dance of the 8 Steps</b><br /> Mind *, Correspondence *, Forces *<br /> This rote, almost always coincidental is virtually indistinguishable from Hu's martial arts. With it he compartmentalises his mind, creating one train of thought for each combatant in the fight. Each mind then observes the combat using correspondence and forces magic to precisely gauge where his opponents are, where they are moving and how fast. This allows him an almost preternatural ability to avoid his enemies blows and to strike them in turn, slipping past blocks and attacking into dodges. In practical terms he enjoys a -1 on the difficulty to dodge and to attack when in combat for each success (will probably need a success for duration too). Attackers who he is unaware of are not subject to this as he won't have created a mind track for them. He can monitor one opponent for each success on his casting roll.<br /> <b>Foci</b>: Martial Arts - Hu takes a sharp breath in and exhales while stepping through the 8 positions of combat taught by the Kuei Lung Chuan making note of each combatant.<br /> <br /> <b>Death of Demons</b><br /> Prime **<br /> Demons (such as vampires, wraiths, fallen magi, shapeshifters, etc) are notoriously hard to kill with normal weapons. Therefore Hu enchants all his weapons with this effect, renewing it weekly.<br /> <b>Foci</b>: Alchemy - Hu washes the weapon in a mix of prepared oils and spring water and then burns a piece of paper with the kanji for ruin and death under the blade so that its smoke is absorbed into the weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Shirt Technique</b><br /> Life ***<br /> This common combat rote is unobtrusive, useful and handy for ambushes. Once cast, it provides lethal soak equal to the casters stamina. Hu casts the rote via a series of kata focused around bringing his yin chi to the surface of his skin, and deep breathing exercises to lock it in place. Hu is generally a yang driven person so he finds this rote slightly distasteful, but cannot deny its usefulness. In more dangerous times, Wu Lung who might reasonably expect trouble would cast this every morning before leaving the safety of their compounds.<br /> <b>Foci</b>: Kuei Lung Chuan katas and deep breathing exercises<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a whole bunch of hard Qigong type techniques you could use too if your paradigm is appropriate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}